meta {
  name: Get Trades
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/trades?limit=50
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  limit: 50
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Get Triggered Trades

  Returns the recent trades the bot triggered, newest first, each tagged with the
  strategy that fired it. Answers "was a trade triggered, and by which strategy?"

  Records every BUY, STOP-SELL, LIMIT-SELL and emergency/manual MARKET-SELL —
  including blocked/failed attempts with the reason (e.g. SHORT_BLOCKED,
  TRADING_HALTED, INSUFFICIENT_BUYING_POWER).

  ## Query
  - `limit` — max entries to return (default 50; buffer keeps the last 500)

  ## Response
  { count, trades: [ { timestamp (UTC), timestampEt (America/New_York), strategy,
    action, ticker, quantity, price, orderType, clientOrderId, orderId, mode,
    success, message } ], timestamp }

  Note: the application runs in ET (America/New_York). Response `timestamp`
  fields are formatted in ET; each trade also carries `timestamp` (UTC) and
  `timestampEt` (ET).

  Strategy values include "600-EMA Momentum", "100/20-EMA Crossover", and system
  sources like "RISK_MANAGER" and "MANUAL_CLOSE_ALL".
}
